---
title: Modifiers
description: Transform modifiers that constrain or snap ghost movement during drag.
---

# Modifiers

Modifiers are functions applied to the ghost's transform on every pointer move. They can restrict, snap, or otherwise transform the drag position before it is applied.

## Built-in modifiers

| Modifier | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `restrictToVerticalAxis` | Locks horizontal movement — ghost only moves up/down |
| `restrictToHorizontalAxis` | Locks vertical movement — ghost only moves left/right |
| `restrictToContainer` | Clamps ghost inside its origin container's bounding box |
| `snapToGrid` | Snaps ghost position to a configurable grid |

All are exported from `@horuse/svelte-dnd`.

## Usage

Pass modifiers to `DndController`:

```ts
import {
    DndController,
    restrictToVerticalAxis,
    snapToGrid,
} from '@horuse/svelte-dnd';

const controller = new DndController({
    modifiers: [restrictToVerticalAxis],
});
```

Modifiers run in array order — each receives the output of the previous.

## snapToGrid

```ts
import { snapToGrid } from '@horuse/svelte-dnd';

const controller = new DndController({
    modifiers: [snapToGrid({ x: 20, y: 20 })],
});
```

Grid cell size is in pixels. Pass `{ x, y }` for non-square grids.

## Combining modifiers

```ts
const controller = new DndController({
    modifiers: [restrictToContainer, snapToGrid({ x: 10, y: 10 })],
});
```

## Custom modifier

Implement `Modifier` to write your own:

```ts
import type { Modifier, ModifierContext } from '@horuse/svelte-dnd';

const clampToPositive: Modifier = ({ transform }) => ({
    x: Math.max(0, transform.x),
    y: Math.max(0, transform.y),
});

const controller = new DndController({
    modifiers: [clampToPositive],
});
```

## Types

```ts
type Modifier = (context: ModifierContext) => { x: number; y: number };

interface ModifierContext {
    /** Current accumulated transform (after previous modifiers) */
    transform: { x: number; y: number };
    /** Transform at the moment drag started */
    initialTransform: { x: number; y: number };
    /** Width/height of the ghost element */
    ghostSize: { width: number; height: number };
}
```

